# Varza design

Varza gets people off the couch to play, socialize, and meet someone new. Rainy Saturday, bored at home, open Varza, see what is on nearby, go. Pitch green is the brand. The logged-in app stays calmer than the marketing pages.

Copy: follow the `varza-voice` skill before any user-facing text. Screen structure: follow the `varza-ux` skill. A new activity: follow the `varza-new-activity` skill.

Do not describe Varza as a tool for ten friends, a small crew, or a WhatsApp replacement. Do not mention WhatsApp on the homepage. The share button inside a game may still say "Share on WhatsApp".

## Voice

Warm, social, a bit cheeky. Second person. Plain English. No exclamation marks. Buttons are verbs: "I'm in", "See what's on", "Start a game". The long before-and-after list is in the voice skill.

Spirit: "Bored at home? Go play."

Locked strings, until a copy change updates the tests too: "Your next game", "Open near you", "Vote on a time", "Availability", "Best time", "Your RSVP", "Lock in this time", "This time has passed".

## Color

Tokens live in `resources/css/app.css` as CSS variables and are mapped in `tailwind.config.js`. Channel variables (`--pitch-700: 28 99 59`) feed Tailwind as `rgb(var(--pitch-700) / <alpha-value>)`, so opacity modifiers such as `bg-pitch-950/40` work. The `--color-*` variables are the same colors without an alpha, for plain CSS.

- Pitch green scale `pitch-50`–`pitch-950`. Primary buttons, links, and focus rings use `pitch-700`. Hover uses `pitch-800`. Soft fills use `pitch-50` and `pitch-100`.
- Neutrals: `canvas` page background, `ink` text, `ink-muted` secondary text, `ink-faint` placeholders, `line` borders, `sand` inside illustrations.
- Status: `success` (same green family), `warn`, `danger`, each with a `soft` background.
- Activity accents are allowed only on chips, tints, and illustrations. Name them as `--activity-*` channel tokens. One accent per activity. Never as a button, body text, or full-page background. Pitch green stays the primary button.
- Do not use Tailwind's default rainbow classes (`indigo`, `orange`, `sky`, `rose`, and the rest). Extra hues go through an `--activity-*` token.

Logged-in screens use canvas and white cards. No mesh, grain, or glass there.

## Marketing pages

Public and marketing pages only (the homepage, not the logged-in app):

- A pitch-green gradient or mesh background: `.bg-pitch-mesh` (`.bg-pitch-wash` remains).
- A subtle grain overlay: `.bg-grain`.
- One dark `pitch-950` band: `.bg-pitch-band`.
- Glassy cards: `.glass-card`.
- Larger headlines than the app: `text-5xl` or `text-6xl`, still Inter, still `font-semibold tracking-tight`.

One dark band, not a dark theme. The rest of the page stays light.

## Typography

Inter, self-hosted in `public/fonts`, with the system sans fallback. Weights in use: 400, 500, 600, 700.

Type scale, already mapped onto Tailwind's text sizes: xs 12, sm 14, base 16, lg 18, xl 20, 2xl 24, 3xl 30, 4xl 36, 5xl 48, 6xl 60. App page titles are `text-2xl` or `text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight`. Marketing headlines may use `text-5xl` or `text-6xl`. Body copy is `text-base` or `text-sm` with `text-ink-muted`. Do not set a font below 16px on inputs (iOS zoom).

## Spacing

Use the 4px scale: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16 (`--space-*`). Stack related items with `gap` or `space-y-*`, not ad-hoc margins between siblings. Page content is `max-w-content` (40rem), padded `px-4` on mobile. Touch targets are at least 44px (`min-h-11`).

## Radius and shadow

- `rounded-control` (12px) on inputs, buttons, and chips.
- `rounded-card` (16px) on cards, illustrations, and menus.
- `rounded-full` on badges, avatars, and activity chips.
- `shadow-card` for resting surfaces. `shadow-lift` for popovers and hovered cards. Prefer a `ring-1 ring-line` over a heavy shadow.

## Icons

One set: [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) (ISC). Outline, 24px viewBox, stroke 2, `currentColor`, round caps and joins.

Render icons only as `<x-ui.icon name="..." />`. Paths in that component are Lucide. Do not add `blade-heroicons`, `blade-lucide-icons`, emoji, or one-off SVG icons in a page. Add a new Lucide path to `x-ui.icon` when a screen needs a new symbol.

Info-row names the UX skill expects: `calendar`, `clock`, `map-pin`, `users`, `signal`, `sun`, `home`.

## Motion

A small kit, CSS and Alpine only. No GSAP, Motion One, anime.js, AOS, or other animation libraries. Durations 150–400ms.

- Press: `.motion-press` scales to 0.98 on active, 150ms. Buttons already use it.
- Success pop: `.motion-pop`, a one-shot scale from 0.96 to 1, 200ms.
- Sliding active indicator: `.motion-slide`, transform, 200ms.
- Count tick: a number changes with a short vertical slide, about 200ms.
- Skeleton pulse: `.motion-skeleton`, opacity only, about 1.2s, and only while loading.
- View transitions: `.motion-view` opts one element in. Do not set it on two elements.
- Hero entrance: marketing pages only, a short staggered fade-up, 400ms total.

`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is handled globally in `app.css`. Do not override it. Under reduced motion: no transform, no pulse, no entrance, instant state. The logged-in app does not use the hero entrance.

## Components

Use these Blade components instead of restyling raw elements.

| Component | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `x-ui.shell` | Logged-in chrome: wordmark, desktop links, account menu, mobile bottom nav. The app layout already wraps it. |
| `x-ui.wordmark` | The mark plus the word Varza. Link it home. |
| `x-ui.page-header` | The title of a screen, with optional subtitle and `actions` slot. |
| `x-ui.section` | A labeled group on a page. |
| `x-ui.card` | A white surface for a form, a detail block, or a poll option. |
| `x-ui.button` | `primary`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `danger`. Pass `href` for a link. Primary is the one next step. Includes `.motion-press`. |
| `x-ui.info-row` | Icon plus text. Variants: `date`, `time`, `place`, `spots`, `level`, `outdoor`, `indoor`. `place` takes `href` for the map. |
| `x-ui.game-card` | One game: illustration, chip, title, info rows, map link outside the title link. |
| `x-ui.chip` | Activity name with that activity's soft accent. |
| `x-ui.label` | Every control's label. |
| `x-ui.input` | Text, email, password, number, date. |
| `x-ui.select` | A native select when there are many short options and chips would wrap into a mess. |
| `x-ui.textarea` | Notes and descriptions. |
| `x-ui.error` | Validation messages for one field. |
| `x-ui.badge` | Status such as "Vote on a time" or "Best time". Tones: `pitch`, `warn`, `neutral`. Presets: `full`, `beginners`, `indoor`, `outdoor`. |
| `x-ui.sport-chip` | The activity name. Delegates to `x-ui.chip`. |
| `x-ui.avatar` | Photo, or initials from a person's name. |
| `x-ui.empty-state` | A titled empty list with an illustration and an optional action. |
| `x-ui.icon` | The Lucide set. |
| `x-illustrations.hero` | Landing hero only. |
| `x-illustrations.sport` | Event cards and the event page. Pass the activity key. |
| `x-illustrations.empty` | Empty states. Variants: `games`, `public`, `invites`, `votes`. |

Illustrations are inline SVG, flat. Pitch green, white, ink, sand, plus that activity's one accent. No stock photos, no hotlinked images.

## Checklist

Point at the one primary action. Facts are info rows. Marketing flourishes stay off the logged-in app. Then run the `varza-voice` and `varza-ux` checklists.
